      "side": 1,
      "message": "does this mean you are prefetching all the mmio registers from crosvm ahead of time? how do you maintain causality?\n\nif the guest does `read register_x` -\u003e `write register_y` -\u003e `read register_z`, do you block the final read until after crosvm witnesses the write and you refresh the gunyah\u0027s view of `register_z`?",
